# TUI

## Workers and loading

- Filesystem and service calls run in Textual workers, not on the UI thread
- Use existing load-generation / token pattern (`LoadTokenMixin`) — stale worker results are ignored
- Do not misuse `call_from_thread` for mutation paths

## Mutation policy

- After operation lock or transaction start, do not cancel the worker — follow existing cancellation policy
- Operation screens block close during active writes

## UX requirements

- Support keyboard and mouse navigation
- Handle loading, empty, and controlled error states — no tracebacks in user-facing errors
- Test at **80×24** minimum; also exercise wider sizes when layout-sensitive

## Testing

- Ordinary UI flows: `tests/tui/fake_service.py` — no real dictionaries
- Safety integration: real core with synthetic fixtures (`tests/test_tui_mutation_safety.py`, `tests/test_tui_recovery_safety.py`)
- Architecture guards: `tests/tui/test_architecture.py`

Screen map: `@docs/TUI_IMPLEMENTATION.md`
